The table box of an inline table takes the width its wrapper was
given, and lays its columns out in that width. Gecko does the same: Its
nsTableFrame::ComputeAutoSize() fits an auto-width table to the
available inline size. So does WebKit’s RenderTable::
updateLogicalWidth(), which clamps an auto width to the containing
block’s content width, and Blink’s ComputeAssignableTableInlineSize(),
which works from the constraint space’s available inline size, while
measuring the table’s min- and max-content sizes separately.
